1
00:00:24,220 --> 00:00:25,620
You catch anything?

2
00:00:30,840 --> 00:00:33,781
Sorry, I didn't mean to
sneak up on you like that.

3
00:00:39,260 --> 00:00:41,600
My name's Nishida, and I'm a fisherman.

4
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:43,620
In the game, anyway.

5
00:00:44,080 --> 00:00:45,017
Back in Japan,

6
00:00:45,100 --> 00:00:49,577
I was the head of network security for a
company called Toto High Speed Internet.

7
00:00:49,660 --> 00:00:50,680
I'm Kirito.

8
00:00:51,320 --> 00:00:54,540
Wait, wasn't Toto the company that... Yep.

9
00:00:54,880 --> 00:00:58,527
We were the folks in charge of
network security for this game.

10
00:01:03,560 --> 00:01:04,600
It's a big one!

11
00:01:05,420 --> 00:01:07,240
Yeah, but I've cut bigger.

12
00:01:09,720 --> 00:01:10,550
Whoa!

13
00:01:13,120 --> 00:01:14,120
Awesome. Thanks.

14
00:01:15,120 --> 00:01:17,097
I'm good at catching
them, but cooking them?

15
00:01:17,180 --> 00:01:18,260
Yeah, not so good.

16
00:01:18,980 --> 00:01:21,677
I'd love to make sashimi
or a nice stew out of them,

17
00:01:21,760 --> 00:01:24,878
But what's the point when
I don't have any soy sauce?

18
00:01:25,060 --> 00:01:29,937
I could go for fish baked with soy sauce
right now, or with radishes with soy sauce.

19
00:01:30,020 --> 00:01:33,837
Hey, if you want, I just might be
able to help you out with that.

20
00:01:33,920 --> 00:01:35,260
Wait, say what?

21
00:02:15,700 --> 00:02:20,077
Here is my heart, I can't see my heart.

22
00:02:20,160 --> 00:02:24,037
I'm in the dream. I'm in the dream.

23
00:02:24,120 --> 00:02:28,097
I'm in the body.

24
00:02:28,180 --> 00:02:30,457
I'm in the body. I'm in the body.

25
00:02:30,540 --> 00:02:34,177
I'm in the

26
00:02:38,380 --> 00:02:40,597
I'm in the body.

27
00:02:40,680 --> 00:02:44,957
I'm in the body.

28
00:02:56,040 --> 00:02:59,077
I wanna always be waiting.

29
00:02:59,160 --> 00:03:02,120
I'll give you everything I have.

30
00:03:15,040 --> 00:03:16,393
It was an amazing meal.

31
00:03:16,580 --> 00:03:19,639
I had no idea you could get
soy sauce in this world.

32
00:03:20,220 --> 00:03:21,808
Actually, I made it myself.

33
00:03:21,980 --> 00:03:24,017
If you want, you can
take some home with you.

34
00:03:24,100 --> 00:03:24,930
Really?

35
00:03:25,080 --> 00:03:28,100
Man, my taste buds bow down before you.

36
00:03:29,200 --> 00:03:30,360
Glad you liked it.

37
00:03:30,580 --> 00:03:33,097
By the way, how high
is your fishing skill?

38
00:03:33,180 --> 00:03:37,004
I'm asking because Kirito hasn't
been able to catch anything yet.

39
00:03:38,560 --> 00:03:42,384
Yeah, well, maybe if all the lakes
on this floor weren't so hard.

40
00:03:43,040 --> 00:03:44,922
Well, actually, that's not true.

41
00:03:45,040 --> 00:03:46,840
As far as fishing goes,

42
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:50,617
the only lake that's tough to catch anything
in is the big one you were at today.

43
00:03:50,700 --> 00:03:51,530
What?

44
00:03:51,900 --> 00:03:54,160
Why would someone design it like that?

45
00:03:54,480 --> 00:03:55,860
Yes, good question.

46
00:03:56,620 --> 00:04:02,060
That lake is the home of the
king of all fish. Seriously?

47
00:04:03,140 --> 00:04:04,940
Yep, we're old pals.

48
00:04:05,340 --> 00:04:08,057
I've had him on the end of
my hook quite a few times.

49
00:04:08,140 --> 00:04:12,316
But he's so strong, he yanks the pool
right out of my hands every time.

50
00:04:15,040 --> 00:04:18,400
I was wondering, do you
have any plans for tomorrow?

51
00:04:24,900 --> 00:04:26,977
I don't mind helping the old guy out,

52
00:04:27,060 --> 00:04:30,457
but how am I supposed to do a
switch move with a fishing pole?

53
00:04:30,540 --> 00:04:33,422
You're the only one I know
who can figure it out.

54
00:04:37,560 --> 00:04:38,777
What if you catch it?

55
00:04:38,860 --> 00:04:39,860
Will you keep it?

56
00:04:40,020 --> 00:04:41,420
Is that even possible?

57
00:04:47,580 --> 00:04:50,109
He is pretty cool,
though, don't you think?

58
00:04:50,580 --> 00:04:53,874
When you both showed up, I
was like, who is this person?

59
00:04:56,400 --> 00:05:00,240
Isn't it funny how people are
living normal lives in this world?

60
00:05:01,140 --> 00:05:03,728
And since we're the
ones on the front lines,

61
00:05:03,980 --> 00:05:07,804
their lives have sort of become
our responsibility, haven't they?

62
00:05:08,900 --> 00:05:12,717
For me, I wasn't getting
stronger for anyone else.

63
00:05:12,800 --> 00:05:15,280
It was just about me staying alive.

64
00:05:20,260 --> 00:05:22,789
Everyone expects great
things from you now.

65
00:05:22,980 --> 00:05:24,640
And guess what? So do I.

66
00:05:25,700 --> 00:05:27,171
Talk about pressure, huh?

67
00:05:29,880 --> 00:05:32,660
Yeah, I promised I'd save everyone.

68
00:05:33,520 --> 00:05:35,285
Hell of a thing to live up to.

69
00:05:37,880 --> 00:05:38,760
Oh, well.

70
00:05:39,580 --> 00:05:41,737
They'll understand if
you take tonight off.

71
00:05:41,820 --> 00:05:42,880
Yeah.

72
00:05:52,160 --> 00:05:53,840
Oh, my God.

73
00:05:54,480 --> 00:05:57,127
Can you believe all the
people who showed up?

74
00:05:59,400 --> 00:06:01,000
Well, here we go.

75
00:06:01,500 --> 00:06:03,417
Thanks for your patience, everyone.

76
00:06:03,500 --> 00:06:05,137
Here comes today's main event.

77
00:06:05,220 --> 00:06:06,280
It's about time.

78
00:06:06,640 --> 00:06:09,560
Kirito, let's catch us a fish. Yeah.

79
00:06:12,780 --> 00:06:15,368
How big is this thing
supposed to be anyway?

80
00:06:16,380 --> 00:06:18,220
Okay, here goes nothing!

81
00:06:42,400 --> 00:06:44,940
Um, shouldn't you reel it in? No, not yet!

82
00:06:46,940 --> 00:06:49,020
Uh, Nishida? Hang on.

83
00:06:49,240 --> 00:06:50,120
Not yet.

84
00:06:52,640 --> 00:06:53,470
Now!

85
00:06:53,700 --> 00:06:55,140
I got this sucker!

86
00:06:58,240 --> 00:06:59,300
Uh, switch?

87
00:07:04,240 --> 00:07:06,560
Call me here, you bastard!

88
00:07:09,820 --> 00:07:10,650
Look!

89
00:07:10,733 --> 00:07:11,582
It's coming up!

90
00:07:18,860 --> 00:07:20,740
I think I tired him out.

91
00:07:23,360 --> 00:07:25,120
Where are you going? Hey!

92
00:07:29,640 --> 00:07:30,980
No, no, no, no!

93
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:32,830
Gito!

94
00:07:33,400 --> 00:07:34,360
Look out!

95
00:07:36,260 --> 00:07:37,280
For what?

96
00:07:51,320 --> 00:07:52,480
You ran away!

97
00:07:52,680 --> 00:07:54,151
You left me there to die!

98
00:07:54,760 --> 00:07:55,940
Here it comes!

99
00:07:57,800 --> 00:07:59,140
Whoa, we can run?

100
00:08:00,220 --> 00:08:02,860
It's like a crazy lungfish. Kirito!

101
00:08:03,040 --> 00:08:04,020
This is serious!

102
00:08:04,220 --> 00:08:05,637
That thing's coming for us!

103
00:08:05,720 --> 00:08:06,896
Hurry, do something!

104
00:08:07,180 --> 00:08:08,680
Yeah, I'm still thinking.

105
00:08:09,560 --> 00:08:11,266
Guess I'll take care of this.

106
00:08:14,400 --> 00:08:16,180
Run while you still can!

107
00:08:16,460 --> 00:08:17,660
Nah, she'll be fine.

108
00:08:19,080 --> 00:08:20,940
Save your wife, Kiri-go!

109
00:08:22,840 --> 00:08:23,960
No! Watch out!

110
00:08:36,160 --> 00:08:37,380
Oh, wow.

111
00:08:38,320 --> 00:08:39,600
That was badass!

112
00:08:40,280 --> 00:08:41,600
You're Asuna, right?

113
00:08:42,160 --> 00:08:43,257
What are you doing here?

114
00:08:43,340 --> 00:08:44,437
Man, this is awesome.

115
00:08:44,520 --> 00:08:45,873
I'm a big fan of yours.

116
00:08:46,100 --> 00:08:47,394
Can I shake your hand?

117
00:08:49,180 --> 00:08:50,340
Nice job, honey.

118
00:08:53,860 --> 00:08:54,690
Heathcliff.

119
00:09:02,900 --> 00:09:03,730
Come on.

120
00:09:03,920 --> 00:09:05,717
You've moped long enough already.

121
00:09:05,800 --> 00:09:08,560
I know, but it's only been two weeks.

122
00:09:08,960 --> 00:09:12,177
If he needs us on the front lines,
then something must have happened.

123
00:09:12,260 --> 00:09:14,672
Why else would he interrupt our vacation?

124
00:09:15,240 --> 00:09:16,560
Yeah, but still.

125
00:09:17,040 --> 00:09:19,452
Let's at least hear what he's got to say.

126
00:09:20,300 --> 00:09:21,476
Come on, time to go.

127
00:09:27,920 --> 00:09:31,200
We'll take care of this,
then come back. You got it.

128
00:09:34,680 --> 00:09:36,151
Thanks for seeing us off.

129
00:09:36,380 --> 00:09:40,204
I know we didn't get to spend much
time together, but it was fun.

130
00:09:40,500 --> 00:09:43,240
Oh, well, it was an honor and a privilege.

131
00:09:44,240 --> 00:09:46,357
Actually, before I met the two of you,

132
00:09:46,440 --> 00:09:49,897
I couldn't imagine what the folks
working to clear the game were like.

133
00:09:49,980 --> 00:09:52,804
You might as well have
been from another planet.

134
00:09:53,540 --> 00:09:56,187
Being trapped in here
for the past two years,

135
00:09:57,320 --> 00:09:59,100
even if I made it out alive,

136
00:09:59,420 --> 00:10:02,980
I don't know if I can go back
to my old job, my old life.

137
00:10:03,500 --> 00:10:07,280
Maybe deep down inside, I've
given up hope of ever getting out.

138
00:10:07,860 --> 00:10:09,917
I figured spending my
time with a fishing pole

139
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:12,700
between my mitts was
the best thing for me.

140
00:10:13,260 --> 00:10:14,220
Pretty sad, huh?

141
00:10:14,940 --> 00:10:15,770
Uh-uh.

142
00:10:15,853 --> 00:10:16,800
That isn't sad.

143
00:10:17,220 --> 00:10:18,396
I get what you mean.

144
00:10:19,580 --> 00:10:22,460
I used to feel the same
as you, at first anyway.

145
00:10:22,960 --> 00:10:24,700
I felt lost and hopeless.

146
00:10:25,240 --> 00:10:27,500
Every night I'd cry myself to sleep.

147
00:10:27,920 --> 00:10:32,744
It felt like each day that went by in here
was another day lost from my real life.

148
00:10:34,140 --> 00:10:38,357
so I'd cry and afterwards I'd
go and fight as hard as I could.

149
00:10:38,440 --> 00:10:40,437
All I cared about was winning.

150
00:10:40,520 --> 00:10:42,617
Getting stronger and
getting to the next floor,

151
00:10:42,700 --> 00:10:48,117
but then I was walking along and I
saw someone taking a nap in the shade.

152
00:10:48,200 --> 00:10:53,220
I was so mad, I told him he
shouldn't waste his time like that.

153
00:10:54,360 --> 00:10:55,417
And then he said,

154
00:10:55,500 --> 00:10:58,177
"and I'll never forget it—this
is aincrad's best season—and

155
00:10:58,260 --> 00:11:00,757
today's weather is?" weather is
He said it's optimal setting.

156
00:11:00,840 --> 00:11:05,075
He said it'd be a waste to go into
some dungeon on such a beautiful day.

157
00:11:05,460 --> 00:11:08,017
So I tried lying down
too, and you know what?

158
00:11:08,100 --> 00:11:09,340
I slept like a baby.

159
00:11:10,500 --> 00:11:14,618
When I woke up, it was evening and
he was giving me the weirdest look.

160
00:11:15,740 --> 00:11:19,858
Anyway, we formed our own party, and
that's when I realized something.

161
00:11:20,980 --> 00:11:24,440
Even in a world like this,
he was really living.

162
00:11:25,380 --> 00:11:27,637
He wasn't losing a day in the real world.

163
00:11:27,720 --> 00:11:30,220
He was gaining a day. Here.

164
00:11:31,180 --> 00:11:33,080
I learned so much from him.

165
00:11:33,460 --> 00:11:35,340
And by him, I mean Kirito.

166
00:11:36,280 --> 00:11:38,957
When I thought about him
before falling asleep,

167
00:11:39,040 --> 00:11:41,216
I noticed I wouldn't have nightmares.

168
00:11:41,460 --> 00:11:44,048
I began looking forward
to seeing him again.

169
00:11:44,720 --> 00:11:49,360
It was like, for the first
time, I was glad I was here.

170
00:11:50,960 --> 00:11:52,620
Kirito was everything to me.

171
00:11:53,960 --> 00:11:55,917
He's what the last two years were about.

172
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:58,480
He's proof I'm alive.

173
00:12:00,480 --> 00:12:02,377
Why'd I put on the nerve gear that day?

174
00:12:02,460 --> 00:12:06,360
It's obvious, so I could
come here and meet him.

175
00:12:07,480 --> 00:12:08,917
You're still alive, right?

176
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:11,680
You must have something to live for too.

177
00:12:12,840 --> 00:12:13,957
Yeah, you're right.

178
00:12:14,040 --> 00:12:16,397
Yeah, you're absolutely right.

179
00:12:16,480 --> 00:12:18,997
Life isn't so bad here.

180
00:12:19,080 --> 00:12:21,280
No, it's actually pretty.

181
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:28,657
I wish there was something I could
do to help, but well, there it is.

182
00:12:28,740 --> 00:12:31,020
Good luck and be safe. Don't worry.

183
00:12:31,420 --> 00:12:32,780
We'll go fishing again.

184
00:12:33,440 --> 00:12:34,540
Take care, okay?

185
00:12:39,220 --> 00:12:40,220
Teleport Gransom!

186
00:12:53,940 --> 00:12:56,180
The recon team was wiped out?

187
00:12:56,480 --> 00:12:58,897
They were scouting for
the upcoming boss fight.

188
00:12:58,980 --> 00:13:02,686
It was a party of 20 members,
taken from five different guilds.

189
00:13:03,340 --> 00:13:05,837
Ten of them reached
the center of the room.

190
00:13:05,920 --> 00:13:07,273
Then the boss appeared.

191
00:13:08,340 --> 00:13:13,105
And that's when the entrance closed,
cutting them off from the rest of the party.

192
00:13:13,960 --> 00:13:16,420
They walked into an anti-crystal zone.

193
00:13:17,080 --> 00:13:17,910
Precisely.

194
00:13:17,993 --> 00:13:22,581
and it couldn't have been more than five
minutes or so when the door finally opened.

195
00:13:22,940 --> 00:13:24,360
The room was empty.

196
00:13:24,640 --> 00:13:30,080
There wasn't any trace left behind of the
ten soldiers, or the boss. You're kidding!

197
00:13:30,420 --> 00:13:34,237
Now more than ever, clearing the game
should be everyone's number one priority.

198
00:13:34,320 --> 00:13:37,737
We're going to launch an attack with
the largest group we can assemble.

199
00:13:37,820 --> 00:13:42,360
You can count on us to fight with
you, but this needs to be clear.

200
00:13:42,700 --> 00:13:44,277
Austin's safety is my priority.

201
00:13:44,360 --> 00:13:48,125
If things start to get hairy in
there, I'm going to protect her.

202
00:13:48,480 --> 00:13:49,774
That's not negotiable.

203
00:13:50,340 --> 00:13:53,869
A person with something to
protect is a strong ally to have.

204
00:13:54,320 --> 00:13:56,438
I'm expecting a good fight from you.

205
00:14:01,080 --> 00:14:02,727
Three more hours of waiting.

206
00:14:03,720 --> 00:14:04,840
What should we do?

207
00:14:08,960 --> 00:14:10,254
What's wrong with you?

208
00:14:12,400 --> 00:14:14,518
There's something I have to ask you.

209
00:14:14,700 --> 00:14:16,994
But I don't want you getting mad at me.

210
00:14:17,680 --> 00:14:21,440
Instead of going to the boss
fight, could you please stay here?

211
00:14:22,740 --> 00:14:24,140
Why would you ask that?

212
00:14:24,840 --> 00:14:29,722
We won't be able to use teleport crystals,
so there's no telling what could happen.

213
00:14:30,520 --> 00:14:31,440
I'm scared.

214
00:14:31,940 --> 00:14:36,680
If anything happened to you, I— So you
want to go to someplace dangerous, alone,

215
00:14:37,160 --> 00:14:39,984
and you expect me to stay
here, where it's safe?

216
00:14:43,520 --> 00:14:46,657
You know what would happen
if you didn't come back, huh?

217
00:14:46,740 --> 00:14:49,620
I'd kill myself.

218
00:14:51,020 --> 00:14:55,844
I'd never forgive myself for staying behind,
so what would be the point in living?

219
00:14:57,300 --> 00:15:02,760
I'm sorry, I guess I'm losing my nerve;
all I want to do is run away with you.

220
00:15:03,520 --> 00:15:06,097
I don't care if we never make
it back to the real world;

221
00:15:06,180 --> 00:15:07,857
I just want to live with you.

222
00:15:07,940 --> 00:15:09,900
in our little house in the woods.

223
00:15:11,640 --> 00:15:13,581
It'd be nice if we could do that.

224
00:15:13,960 --> 00:15:16,360
Be together, every day, forever.

225
00:15:19,120 --> 00:15:22,297
Have you ever thought about what's
happening in the real world?

226
00:15:22,380 --> 00:15:25,733
About what's happening to our
bodies while we're in here?

227
00:15:27,300 --> 00:15:31,037
A few weeks after the game was
launched, do you remember what happened?

228
00:15:31,120 --> 00:15:35,708
Most of the players suddenly went offline
and stayed that way for a few hours.

229
00:15:36,280 --> 00:15:38,817
My guess is that's when
all the players' bodies

230
00:15:38,900 --> 00:15:41,724
were being moved to
hospitals in the real world.

231
00:15:42,440 --> 00:15:45,457
If that's where we all are
right now in hospitals,

232
00:15:45,540 --> 00:15:47,717
barely being kept alive by machines,

233
00:15:47,800 --> 00:15:51,017
it's hard to believe we're going to
survive like that for much longer,

234
00:15:51,100 --> 00:15:56,617
so that means it doesn't matter whether
we clear the game or not anymore.

235
00:15:56,700 --> 00:16:00,960
Everyone here is on a time
limit, and once that's up.

236
00:16:05,400 --> 00:16:06,230
I…

237
00:16:06,313 --> 00:16:07,537
I want to…

238
00:16:07,620 --> 00:16:09,560
to stay with you forever.

239
00:16:12,080 --> 00:16:14,500
I want us to go on real dates.

240
00:16:14,900 --> 00:16:16,680
And to really get married.

241
00:16:17,200 --> 00:16:19,180
And for us to grow old together.

242
00:16:21,400 --> 00:16:22,677
That's why…

243
00:16:22,760 --> 00:16:23,900
that's why…

244
00:16:26,660 --> 00:16:28,300
We don't have a choice.

245
00:16:28,740 --> 00:16:30,440
We have to keep fighting.

246
00:16:52,420 --> 00:16:53,250
Hey!

247
00:16:55,420 --> 00:16:56,250
No way.

248
00:16:56,560 --> 00:16:57,972
You guys are coming too?

249
00:16:58,260 --> 00:16:59,497
That's the best you got?

250
00:16:59,580 --> 00:17:00,410
No way?

251
00:17:00,700 --> 00:17:04,557
Hey, man, I shut my shop down to
come out here and help get this done.

252
00:17:04,640 --> 00:17:08,157
Brother, you're looking at a player who's
about as philanthropic as they come.

253
00:17:08,240 --> 00:17:10,357
Then seeing as how
you're so philanthropic,

254
00:17:10,440 --> 00:17:12,337
